    {
      "findingId": "js-self-profiling-markers-chrome-153",
      "outcome": "investigation-only",
      "facts": [
        "Chrome 153 lists JavaScript Self-Profiling Markers as a new origin trial rather than stable browser shipping.",
        "The marker proposal adds an optional sample category for script, gc, style, layout, paint or other browser work.",
        "Marker access is restricted to cross-origin-isolated contexts, and the base profiler checks the js-profiling-mode or js-profiling Document Policy.",
        "XTend already records stream-pressure samples and exposes performance telemetry snapshots, but it has no JavaScript Self-Profiling or marker ingestion path."
      ],
      "xtendHypotheses": [
        "A future opt-in test-only adapter could correlate aggregated marker categories with existing Fabric lane and backpressure telemetry without exposing trace format or sampling data as a stable runtime contract."
      ],
      "sources": [
        {
          "id": "chrome-153-beta",
