    {
      "findingId": "fetch-request-streaming-webkit-tp250",
      "outcome": "corrected-candidate",
      "facts": [
        "Safari Technology Preview 251 added backpressure when uploading a stream request body with fetch(), but Technology Preview evidence is not stable Safari shipping.",
        "Chromium has shipped request streaming since 105 with duplex: half plus redirect, CORS and HTTP/2-or-newer restrictions.",
        "Firefox request streaming remains an in-development engine issue rather than a shipping feature.",
        "XTend Maraca still sends buffered JSON request envelopes and only streams NDJSON responses; NFM-BPR-019 therefore keeps fetch-request-streaming at reject-for-now."
      ],
      "xtendHypotheses": [
        "A request-side streaming contract may later extend the host-injected Maraca HTTP transport, but the current Search Worker is not the relevant network boundary."
      ],
      "sources": [
        {
          "id": "webkit-tp251",
